    "language": "This makes sense. We-- if the right striker is open, then we want to pass to him, and then once-- and then you want to move to make yourself viable. Now, there's a few things that we should clarify. The first one is, we shou-... You need to get the ball at the start, and so wait until you get the ball to start you- your passes. Next is we wanna pass... look upfield to pass. And so we want to check if the left or right striker is open, and if one of them is open, we pass to them. If not, we want to pass to one of our wingers that's open. Now, moving to the target is good, except we don't need to wait for the receiver to receive the ball before we move. We can move the moment we kick that ball. Um, where we move depends on who we pass to, but the idea is we want to move to create a rough triangle with the three players that are closest to the ball.",
